Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 6, verse 94:

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And you have certainly come to Us alone, as We created you the first time, and you have left behind you what We bestowed upon you; and We do not see with you your intercessors whom you claimed to be partners among you.﴾ (p-488) In this noble verse, He, exalted is He, mentions that the disbelievers will come on the Day of Resurrection, each one of them alone, without their partners with them. He, exalted is He, stated explicitly that each one comes individually in His saying: ﴿And all of them will come to Him on the Day of Resurrection, alone﴾ [Maryam: 95], and in His saying in this verse: ﴿as We created you the first time﴾ [al-An'am: 94], meaning individually, with no wealth, no goods, no slaves, and no servants with you, barefoot, naked, uncircumcised (ghurlan), meaning not circumcised: ﴿As We began the first creation, We will repeat it; a promise upon Us. Indeed, We are ever doing it﴾ [al-Anbiya': 104]. You have come to know from the verse that the singular of al-Furada (those who come alone) is fard (alone), and it is also said fardan (with a fatha on the ra' in the sense of a single one), and from it is the saying of al-Nabigha Dhubyani [Basit meter]:

From wild cattle and a spotted she-ass whose legs are striped, lean of belly, like the sword of the polisher, the single (fard) one.

* *

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Certainly your relations have been severed from you, and what you used to claim has strayed from you.﴾ In this noble verse, He mentions that the rivals they used to worship in the world will stray from them on the Day of Resurrection, and the ties that existed between them and those rivals in the world will be cut off. He clarified this meaning in very many verses:

• Such as His saying: ﴿And when mankind are gathered, they will be enemies to them and will deny their worship﴾ [al-Ahqaf: 6];

• and His saying: ﴿No! They will deny their worship of them and will become opponents to them﴾ [Maryam: 82];

• and His saying: ﴿You have only taken, other than Allah, idols as a bond of affection among yourselves in the life of this world; then on the Day of Resurrection, some of you will deny others and some of you will curse others, and your refuge will be the Fire, and you will have no helpers﴾ [al-'Ankabut: 25];

• and His saying: ﴿Where is that which you used to worship, other than Allah? Can they help you or defend themselves?﴾ [al-Shu'ara': 92–93];

• and His saying here: ﴿and We do not see with you your intercessors whom you claimed﴾ [al-An'am: 94].
